From f67e82cbe5faabd731dbcc904b9e6c22e7139cca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Moss Heim <moss.heim@qt.io>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:56:10 +0200
Subject: [sbom] Include missing pdfium dependencies

Because SBOM dep tracking uses `gn desc deps`, which lists build files
with dependencies used in the target, 3rdparty dependencies defined in
pdfium/third_party/BUILD.gn such as bigint are missed, even though they
are compiled and their directories contain README.pdfium.

To get around this, make a stub BUILD.gn in each directory with a dummy
empty source_set dependency, and include it as a dependency of the
corresponding vendored dep in pdfium/third_party/BUILD.gn. This causes
gn to list it as a dependency when it's used, and then
licenses.py and sbom.py pull in the metadata.

We also backport the missing README.pdfium file for bigint from
upstream (pdfium commit 47449e8970720ccaba6ce03e49539162c9f70da8).

